ve to you know  respond to these prompts especially as a  beginner when I can't do them I believe  that based on the little reading I've  done on on  the brain works and especially the  function of our mirror neurons that as  we get more and more exposure to the  language our ability to anticipate  improves and that I gather that if we  are used to listening to a language  Russian Chinese whatever and we've been  doing a variety of things to help us  notice the language that when we hear it  the neurons fire the same way as if we  were speaking so I have never felt that  there was a great need to start speaking  early I think speaking is a good thing  to do and the amount of speaking should  increase and when we speak we do  discover gaps in our learning so it's  one of these things like flashcard  review like grammar review one of these  things that helped us notice things but  in my way of learning is those of you  who have listened to me before know very  well still focuses largely on input  listening and reading the third thing  they say that's their secret is that  it's organic in other words it's  listening only and they make a big deal  of the fact that human beings were  listening before they were reading true  and so listening is important but I find  it much easier to learn if I can also  read I find that all of these things  help us notice things it helps to make  the vocabulary stick so why would I deny  myself reading and in fact I listen when  I'm doing other chores but if I have  dedicated learning time available I  prefer to read because I believe that my  vocabulary grows more when I read when I  can actually see the word and when we're  learning a language when we read we  always sub vocalize anyway so it's kind  of somewhat almost like listening  assisted listening the fourth thing  again their secret is this core  vocabulary idea which is again very  common people are very concerned to  learn the most common words and if we  are prepared to - it 